<!--Render Target Documentation — LeafOptimization
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.LeafOptimization-->
<rdoc:LeafOptimization xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Direct mb_block call for single-NativeBlock types
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Some block types are a single NativeBlock: every property maps 1:1 to
    native settings, no sub-blocks, no multi-child composition. Example:
    com.machineblocks.bml.bricks.Standard.

    Standalone compile of such a block emits a typed module and a main call of
    that module. The module reads settings with mb_param / mb_param_* and
    forwards them to mb_block(), so a Set can call the same module with size,
    offset, and direction. Customizer variables are the block properties:

        mb__com__machineblocks__scad__bricks__Standard(
            config = mb_config,
            settings = [
                ["size", size],
                ["studs", studs]
            ]
        );

        module mb__com__machineblocks__scad__bricks__Standard(config = undef, settings = undef) {
            size = mb_param_size(config, settings, [4, 2, 3]);
            studs = mb_param_studs(config, settings, true);
            mb_block(
                config = config,
                settings = [
                    ["size", size],
                    ["studs", studs]
                ]
            );
        }

    Composite blocks with real inner structure (Wall, Calibrator) still emit
    the wrapper module in CompositeRendering.

    Exactly one NativeBlock child, and no bml:each, bml:if, or bml:with, uses
    this module. A composition that carries those directives uses the composite
    path so the directives can expand. Zero children returns files: [] and
    diagnostic MB_EMPTY_BLOCK. Two or more children use the composite module.
    A parameter this target cannot lower returns files: [] and diagnostic
    BML_LEAF_VALUE_UNSUPPORTED. The file is not written with an undefined
    variable in its place.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:CompositeRendering" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:LeafOptimization>
